$ ~/.cache

`$HOME/.cache` is the default directory to be used if the environment variable → development/environment-variable#xdg_cache_home[`$XDG_CACHE_HOME`] is not set.

sa:

  The subdirectories
    • `→ Linux/fhs/home/username/_cache/huggingface[huggingface]`
    • `opencode`
    • `→ Linux/fhs/home/username/_cache/pip[pip]`
    • `qmd`

  `→ Linux/fhs/home/username/_cache/fontconfig[fontconfig]`

  `→ Linux/fhs/var/cache`

  `→ Linux/fhs/home/username/_local/share`

  The presense of a `CACHEDIR.TAG` file whose first 43 bytes, encoded in ASCII, are equal to `Signature: 8a477f597d28d172789f06886806bc55` within a given directory
  indicates that the entire contents of that directory,
  including any and all subdirectories underneath it can be regenerated if necessary, see → https://bford.info/cachedir/[bford.info/cachedir].
